{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited","id":599009,"title":"Society, revisited","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-21T21:20:45-07:00","id":599009,"title":"Society, revisited","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is a hack of the setting of Werewolf: the Forsaken. The point of this hack is to shake up the society of werewolves, doing away with the concept of antagonist factions, and broading the thematic focus of the 5 (Forsaken) tribes so as to include the antagonists factions. Why? Because I can. Because it's fun to mess with the settings in new and, hopefully, interesting ways. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Thesis: There are no Pure Tribes. There are no Bale Hounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#500050\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">There are only the 5 known tribes of the Uratha.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The tribes are thematically diverse enough to include philosophies represented by the (official setting) Pure and Bale Hounds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider the Bone Shadows. They hunt spirits, yes, but they also study them, learn from them and respect them (&quot;pay each spirit in kind&quot;). The act of worship of spirits isn't an alien concept to the Uratha, as most packs hunt with a totem spirit. Some Bone Shadows take the idea of worshipping spirits to extremes, devoting themselves to the service of the most powerful of spirit gods, even burning scars of fire into their skin, all to appease their gods and gain their approval, support and protection. It is those Bone Shadows touched by fire who are the most dangerous of them, as their masters often turn them on other packs. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider the Storm Lords. They take pride in their hard duty and in never showing weakness, but that pride sometimes becomes a weakness of its own. Some Storm Lords think they're better than the rest; polishing their claws of ivory as they declare themselves the most noble and pure of all Uratha. It doesn't usually take a long time for &quot;we're better than everyone else&quot; to turn into &quot;everyone else is less deserving than us&quot;. Some Storm Lords choose to take their faith in their own perceived supremacy into action, hunting those they consider weak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider the Hunters in Darkness. Many of them diligently protect places of nature and wild that are sacred to them, turning to their inner wolf for answers, perhaps rejecting a little of their human ancestry as they turn to the Black Wolf. Some develop deep mistrust and hatred of all things human (despoilers of nature, all of them). Some yearn for a different, simpler age, in which they get to live as kings of predators in a world in which there are much fewer of these useless monkeys running around. Some seek to find ways of creating that age. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider the Blood Talons. All of them have made the intentional decision to be closely familiar with rage and violence and bloodshed. Some of them go too far, finding hidden power in their rage that few other werewolves can even consider. Some refuse to control their rage or their more depraved instincts, believing that Fenris wants them to embrace their monstrosity. A few of them find other gods - Asmodai, Queen of Wrath, and Thurifuge, Architect of Violence among them, believing them to be avatars of Fenris himself. These gods never give up the chance to provide Blood Talons with clarity of rage and the satisfaction of tearing apart their enemies. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Consider the Iron Masters. They live among people, often masquerading as men and women. Some of them choose to learn the worst kind of lesson from people, adopting moral weaknesses from their charges - pride, envy, lust, wrath, greed. It is very easy for a wolf to set himself up as a lord of vice. The Iron Masters have all the right tools for preying on men, even if doing so only serves the interests of the pack in question. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The tribal philosophies aren't binary - they're a scale. No werewolf is entirely virtuous or fully depraved. The nastier excesses of the tribe are, however, mostly, socially accepted by the tribe. Death Wolf will not stop werewolves from choosing to serve the darkest spirits. Storm Lords who are supremacists and racists are still part of the tribe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#500050\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">In this setting hack, werewolf society ultimately has less cohesion than in the official setting. The pack is everything - tribes are more creeds and philosophies than societies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Some packs include werewolves on the more extreme end of the tribal philosophies in their numbers. Some packs consist only of extremists. Good luck if your territory borders on land belonging to Hunters in Darkness thinking themselves Predator Kings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Creation myths exist, counting among them the many variants of the Father Wolf myth. Did we kill the Father? Out of pride or to claim his duties? Was he weakened by the Spinner Hag's poison at that time? Does it really matter? No wolf will ever know. The spirits give answers to Bone Shadows readily, but it is all too easy to become ensnared in their lies. Variant faiths exist and prosper. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ultimately, it's all a matter of faith. The setting doesn't have answers, but it has lots of people and creatures and things who benefit from wolves believing their lies (including, possibly, the tribal totems and lunes).</span></span><br /> <br /> Thoughts? Constructive criticism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 07-22-2015, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T01:17:42-07:00","id":599080,"title":"","content":"+1<br /> <br /> I'm not a huge fan of antagonist splats across the board, and the Pure leave a particularly bad taste. What you propose here very closely resembles the setting as I run it, with a focus on the greyzones and unknown (which are, IMO, the heart of personal horror). So count me as a positive vote towards this take on the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:06:57-07:00","id":599349,"title":"","content":"What if you don't fit into one of the tribes or don't want to join them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T07:36:45-07:00","id":599377,"title":"","content":"Another +1.<br /> I like it... Kudos <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T08:34:48-07:00","id":599445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599349#post599349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you don't fit into one of the tribes or don't want to join them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're a Ghost Wolf. Which isn't really a bad thing to be, if your packmates don't mind, and if you don't see anything wrong with you not having the support of a wolf god - representing affinity to a few gift lists, and a few other nice things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:02:53-07:00","id":599642,"title":"","content":"Without the internecine warfare, who do these werewolves fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:30:03-07:00","id":599653,"title":"","content":"Werewolves don't fight wars. They hunt. Prey includes, other than the usual suspects, other werewolf packs you can't play nice with, for all the usual reasons - dogmatic violence, territory disputes, resources, religion, tradition, etc.<br /> <br /> The Pure and the Bale Hounds aren't gone. There just isn't any distinction between the bad guys and the good guys, except on a pack level. A pack composed of, say, Bone Shadows whose spirit lord tells them it wants to feast on your pelts isn't any different from - in the official setting - a pack of Fire Touched who hunt you for similar religious reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:33:48-07:00","id":599656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599642#post599642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without the internecine warfare, who do these werewolves fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>If humans can go to war with one another, even in the absence of unambiguously bad guys, why should Uratha be any different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:34:19-07:00","id":599657,"title":"","content":"... and if the PCs themselves include Bone Shadows as well; yeah. Your tribal totems supports and aids your mortal enemies just as much as it helps you. Doesn't that make you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:34:53-07:00","id":599658,"title":"","content":"In that case I'm curious why you kept the Hunters in Darkness, at least as a tribal name and totem, when they seem to be the weakest thematically, and mostly taken over by Predator King philosophy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599656#post599656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If humans can go to war with one another, even in the absence of unambiguously bad guys, why should Uratha be any different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Uratha aren't human and it's not Human: the Geopoliticking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-22-2015, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:50:43-07:00","id":599670,"title":"","content":"There are a few misconceptions here. They aren't the weakest tribe; thematically. And none of the five tribes' philosophies have been taken over - thematic ground was added to the tribes. None of the old concepts were done away with or don't fit into the tribes anymore. <br /> <br /> The new Hunters in Darkness aren't the Predator Kings. They're a diverse tribe of individuals whose individual viewpoints are on a scale that includes Hunter in Darkness and (official setting) Predator King ideology. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:57:49-07:00","id":599675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599670#post599670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a few misconceptions here. They aren't the weakest tribe; thematically. And none of the five tribes' philosophies have been taken over - thematic ground was added to the tribes. None of the old concepts were done away with or don't fit into the tribes anymore.<br /> <br /> The new Hunters in Darkness aren't the Predator Kings. They're a diverse tribe of individuals whose individual viewpoints are on a scale that includes Hunter in Darkness and (official setting) Predator King ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess whether it's weak, thematically, is arguable then. It seems like the only part that crossed over is the protection of sacred places, something the Predator Kings and almost every other tribe are fond of as well. The rest of the write-up for them describes things more in vein with the Predator Kings, which is what I meant by 'taken over,' in that outside of title they seem more like Predator Kings with some Hunters in Darkness ideology.<br /> <br /> Also, do you see this as making multi-tribe packs more or less common?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-22-2015, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:01:40-07:00","id":599681,"title":"","content":"All of the writeups emphasize those elements of the tribes where antagonist stuff has been added. That's &quot;added&quot;. There's no taking over of conceptual space. The old concepts don't go anywhere.<br /> <br /> About as common as in the official game. Packs form for all kinds of reasons; tribes are only few of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:05:31-07:00","id":599686,"title":"","content":"And protectorates? Would they be more rare with tribes being less of a cohesive force?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:14:58-07:00","id":599715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599686#post599686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And protectorates? Would they be more rare with tribes being less of a cohesive force?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the sheer number of threats in Forsaken alone (sans Pure and Bale Wolves of course) Werewolves still have a lot to contend with. Get into the wider World of Darkness and I dare say they're quite overwhelmed. Protectorates might not need to flex their chops as often, but I can see plenty of reason to keep them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:18:18-07:00","id":599716,"title":"","content":"This is really impressive. I actually thought the Hunter in Darkness-Predator Kings was very clever. One of those things you don't think of until someone points it out, and then it clicks.<br /> <br /> I think the one weakness is the Iron Masters, but it's fairly obvious why that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (sans Pure and Bale Wolves of course) </div> </div> </div>They're still there. Bale Hounds being extremist Blood Talons doesn't make them any less a threat to most other Uratha. Same goes for the Pure factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":178,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","user":"Michael","date":". 07-22-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:24:50-07:00","id":599738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599715#post599715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the sheer number of threats in Forsaken alone (sans Pure and Bale Wolves of course) Werewolves still have a lot to contend with. Get into the wider World of Darkness and I dare say they're quite overwhelmed. Protectorates might not need to flex their chops as often, but I can see plenty of reason to keep them around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing is, there are still Pure and Bale Hounds, they're just not in their own tribes, they're in the five 'Forsaken' ones. In the main setting you have in-fighting within the tribes but generally you can trust other members of your tribe, to an extent. Now you may fall in with a bunch of Bone Shadows who worship some alien god of the Hisil and want you to do so as well, and if not, prepare for torture. And the Bale Hounds have even more room to maneuver, being definitively a lodge or personal choice, as opposed to an obvious Ninth Tribe. So every protectorate can conceivably hold a number of servants of the Maeljin, maneuvering the kingdom into some atrocity or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:58:17-07:00","id":599787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599716#post599716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really impressive. I actually thought the Hunter in Darkness-Predator Kings was very clever. One of those things you don't think of until someone points it out, and then it clicks.<br /> <br /> I think the one weakness is the Iron Masters, but it's fairly obvious why that is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They're still there. Bale Hounds being extremist Blood Talons doesn't make them any less a threat to most other Uratha. Same goes for the Pure factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've tried to integrate the Bale Hounds, who're a pretty diverse bunch in first edition, into the Iron Masters and Blood Talons; but really, the point of this all is that you could fit a very diverse set of beliefs into all 5 tribes. There is absolutely room for Bale Hounds in the other tribes as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:16:21-07:00","id":599814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599738#post599738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, there are still Pure and Bale Hounds, they're just not in their own tribes, they're in the five 'Forsaken' ones. In the main setting you have in-fighting within the tribes but generally you can trust other members of your tribe, to an extent. Now you may fall in with a bunch of Bone Shadows who worship some alien god of the Hisil and want you to do so as well, and if not, prepare for torture. And the Bale Hounds have even more room to maneuver, being definitively a lodge or personal choice, as opposed to an obvious Ninth Tribe. So every protectorate can conceivably hold a number of servants of the Maeljin, maneuvering the kingdom into some atrocity or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether intentional or not, you've just described a game I'd absolutely love to play!<br /> <br /> Honestly though, I see that as a good thing. nWoD has always billed itself as personal horror, and so it's scenarios like this, where it's not the world, or the country, or even city at stake, but merely your character in a dangerous situation, arrived at by a path she believed to be safe, that resonate with that intent.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Plus, it's not like you can't run a classic protectorate, unmarred by Maeljin or alien gods. As Christian A said, tribes are a gradient, and it's possible for a collection of packs to come together on the brighter side of that scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-22-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:22:25-07:00","id":599826,"title":"","content":"Are my posts coming across full of profanity or something? Are racist epithets being inserted between my words? Because I didn't do either.<br /> <br /> I'm just asking questions about a setting hack. I'm undecided on it because it offers a lot of changes to the setting than are described in the original post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:26:54-07:00","id":599827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599826#post599826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are my posts coming across full of profanity or something? Are racist epithets being inserted between my words? Because I didn't do either.<br /> <br /> I'm just asking questions about a setting hack. I'm undecided on it because it offers a lot of changes to the setting than are described in the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. No, no, no. Sorry, that must have sounded pithy. Far from the intent.<br /> <br /> My posts are more me musing about the hacks then attempting to refute or counter your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:32:34-07:00","id":599830,"title":"","content":"Okay, sorry. I know I can come off as brusque but I'm more curious than anything else so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:36:12-07:00","id":599835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/599009-society-revisited?p=599826#post599826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are my posts coming across full of profanity or something? Are racist epithets being inserted between my words? Because I didn't do either.<br /> <br /> I'm just asking questions about a setting hack. I'm undecided on it because it offers a lot of changes to the setting than are described in the original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who are you talking to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:32:27-08:00","id":820142,"title":"","content":"This is an innnnnteresting setting suggestion. It would certainly make things very different in terms of the primary conflict, because it wouldn't come from two discrete and opposite viewpoints and base ideologies but from how each werewolf and tribe deals with the fact that they are <i>all</i> Forsaken in some way for their crime against Father Wolf. Some upholding his duty as his heirs, or seeing it as their right to judge what the spirit world is allowed, some repenting by serving spirits, or pushing up their own egos and denying they have anything to be sorry for, or trying to reclaim the hunter's paradise lost with Urfarah's death. And the bigger differences in opinion would form the divides of the &quot;Pure&quot; against the &quot;Forsaken&quot;, but as <i>internal conflict</i>, rather than focused outwardly.<br /> <br /> I think that there's definitely some loss of distinction in the diversity of things, because even in the standard setting there can be nearly opposite viewpoints inside the Pure or the Forsaken. Not every Pure is a zealot or necessarily misguided, and not every Forsaken cares about the balance or is a good warden of the worlds.<br /> <br /> But what's gained is an inability to clearly define the divisions. The opposite viewpoint can be anyone. It can much more easily be someone in your own pack. Which I guess is a fair trade in terms of writing potential.<br /> <br /> Especially in the context of 2e, I think having only the five Forsaken tribes may dillute some themes, and a few of the suggested relations or conflations seem a bit weak. Particularly with the Iron Masters. But I have to admit the Hunters In Darkness &lt;-&gt; Predator Kings one is really good, because it just clicks. And consideration made it occur to me that the Blood Talons would have <i>much</i> heavier tension with the other tribes due to an absence of clear groups to oppose, which would be funnn. I can also see a much greater focus on oathbreakers as the targets of their sacred hunt.<br /> <br /> Also Lodges, Lodges, LODGES! This would be great for seeing tons of interesting lodges within the tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 01-31-2016, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T21:45:21-08:00","id":820150,"title":"","content":"I see you couldn't help yourself with providing both our feedback from that discussion, YOLF.<br /> <br /> Thank you for saving me the effort!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T22:51:56-08:00","id":820183,"title":"","content":"I like this. A lot. I'm not sold on the idea of reducing the number of Tribes; I think there is still value in having followers of Rabid Wolf, Silver Wolf, and Dire Wolf. But I love the idea of breaking down the division of Pure and Forsaken. To be honest, I've never been a big fan of Bale Hounds (though the &quot;sell me on&quot; thread helps), so I'm not terribly concerned with integrating them into the Forsaken tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":""